    ['id' => 'evaluation', 'title' => 'My annual evaluation', 'body' => [
      'My leave › How we evaluate you explains the whole method and shows your computed scores so far for the running year — read it at the start of the year, not at the end. Once a year your manager (with HR) writes your evaluation: eight criteria scored 1 to 5 — quality of work, productivity, technical skills, teamwork, initiative, reliability, safety & procedures, communication — with strengths, areas to improve, goals for next year and training needs; two more scores are computed by the portal from the year\'s facts — training participation (what you attended, ranked among colleagues) and attendance & consistency (early leaves / late arrivals, unplanned absences, leave asked at the last moment) — and the targets of the year are summed up. When it is final you are notified; read it on My leave › My evaluations, add your own comment if you wish, and press Acknowledge. Acknowledging means you have read it, not necessarily that you agree — write your view in the comment; it stays with the evaluation. Your evaluations of past years stay on the same page.',
