    ['id' => 'requisitions', 'title' => 'Asking for parts — purchase requisitions (v1.91.0)', 'body' => [
      'If your discipline is enabled for requisitions (or you are a PM), the left menu shows Procurement › Requisitions. "+ New requisition": pick the project and sub-project, the purpose (project, stock, service call) and the date you need the parts by; create it, then add the lines — search the inventory by code or description (the picker shows the free stock) or type a free-text line with maker and part number. "Submit to Procurement" freezes the lines; Procurement checks the parts budget of the sub-project and approves (stock reserved, the rest bought), sends it to management if it is over budget, or rejects with a reason — you are notified at every step and can follow the log on the request. The warehouse issues the reserved parts to you; the request closes when every line is issued.',
      'Engineering BOM (v1.92.0): if you are in the team of a sub-project (or your discipline is enabled), the Procurement tab of the sub-project lets you keep its bill of materials as revisions — upload the file or type the lines, see what the stock covers, issue the revision to Procurement, and answer their change proposals (accept or reject with a reason). The approved revision is the current BOM; one click makes a requisition for the lines the stock does not cover.',
      'BOM import (v1.113.0): use the template from the BOM page; after the upload review each row — the portal proposes the inventory item (by Golden code, maker part number or the assistant) with its stock; Accept, Reject (free text), pick another item or create a New inventory item, then Apply.',
      'Goods receipt (v1.94.0, Warehouse flag): on a sent purchase order the Goods receipt box lets you book what arrived per line — received and rejected quantities with the reason (damaged, wrong type, missing) and the action (return, replacement, credit), delivery note and a scan. Accepted parts go into the warehouse at the order price and are reserved for the requisition they were bought for; the requester is told and you issue them from the requisition as usual.',
      'Item documents and software licences (v1.105.0): on an inventory item card you find the links Procurement added — datasheet, manual, drawing, certificate, software download, supplier page. Software items show their licences (product, version, seats, expiry, where assigned); the licence key itself is visible only to procurement administrators. When a delivery note was issued to your project, the goods are already out of the warehouse — the note (number, PDF) is linked on the purchase order receipt and listed under Inventory › Delivery notes.',
      'Parts from the phone (v1.97.0 — Service app 0.6.18, Golden HR 1.0.4; v1.103.1: tap the item box to see the recently used items): Home › 🧾 Parts & requisitions lists your requisitions (Open / Mine / All) and "+ New requisition" raises one from the phone — project, sub-project, purpose, needed-by, title, then lines: search the inventory by code or description, scan the barcode with 📷, or type a free-text part with maker and part number, set the quantity and unit, "+ Add line", and Submit to Procurement. Open a request to follow it: state, every line with reserved · ordered · received · issued, the log of decisions, and Cancel while nothing has been reserved. You need to be online; the same request appears in the browser under Procurement › Requisitions.',
